<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The widget's pane — PrayerTimesCard's GlassCard, rendered where there is no
    compositor to frost with.

    A launcher cannot blur what is behind it, so the two things that make glass
    read as glass in the app are spent differently here:

      * the FILL is the card's translucent white already blended against the
        app's own backdrop (see values/colors.xml), rather than an alpha the
        launcher would resolve against a wallpaper nobody can predict — a pane
        at 80% over a photograph is not a pane, it is a photograph;
      * the SHEEN survives intact, as the 315° fall from pane_start to pane_end.
        It is worth keeping: it is the whole difference between a card and a
        flat swatch, and it costs one gradient.

    Radius is AppRadius.xl, which is what PrayerTimesCard asks its GlassCard for.
    It was 22dp — a value on no scale this app has.

    The hairline is a NEUTRAL at low alpha, not the brand green it used to be.
    GlassTokens.light gives the reason at length: a pane may be washed with a
    tone, this one is washed green whenever a prayer is open, and an edge with a
    hue of its own argues with the wash across one millimetre.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <gradient
        android:angle="315"
        android:startColor="@color/prayer_widget_pane_start"
        android:endColor="@color/prayer_widget_pane_end"
        android:type="linear" />
    <corners android:radius="32dp" />
    <stroke
        android:width="1dp"
        android:color="@color/prayer_widget_stroke" />
</shape>
